Two similar solid metal spheres A and B, each of radius $R$, are situated in a vacuum such that the separation of their centres is $D$, as shown in Fig. 6.1.

{{figure:9702_w18_42_q06_figure_6_1}}

The charge $+Q$ on sphere A is larger than the charge $+q$ on sphere B.

A movable point P is located on the line joining the centres of the two spheres. The point P is a distance $x$ from the centre of sphere A.

On Fig. 6.2, sketch a graph to show the variation with $x$ of the electric potential $V$ between the centres of the two spheres.

{{figure:9702_w18_42_q06_figure_6_2}}
